A1. This is a place where age comes before youth, alimony before divorce and finish before start. ~ DICTIONARY
A9. You would never say this to a lady. ~ SIR
A11. What she found in her stocking on Xmas. ~ RUNS
A12. Rocks in the cradle of the deep. ~ REEFS
A15. An indefinite article. ~ AN
A16. What was Adam a little before Eve? ~ BORN
A17. This has its ups and downs. ~ SEESAW
A18. A peaceful state that Al Smith likes to be in, after the strenuous campaign. (Abbr.) ~ NY
A19. This comes and goes. ~ LUCK
A20. This usually comes with the Spring. ~ TOAD
A21. A bad state to be in. ~ MAD
A23. A tropical plant cultivated for its root stock. ~ TARO
A24. These are growing longer every day. ~ BOBS
A25. The way some football players feel after a game. ~ SORE
A26. Little prophets that come about Feb. 2nd. ~ GROUNDHOGS
A29. You wouldn't want to use this in a pinch. ~ THUMB
A30. This is what Herbert Hoover offered to the people of South America. ~ HAND
A31. The corn state. ~ IOWO
A32. A Greek god. ~ ARES
A33. Attempt. ~ TRY
A34. These are often scaled. ~ ALPS
A35. This has eyes but sees not. ~ SPUD
A36. This is a short measure. (Abbr.) ~ PT
A37. This is a form of the ego. ~ ME
A38. Here is where you find the upper crust. (Plural). ~ PIES
A39. There's no use living without this. ~ HOPE
A40. This is all that came out of the pot. ~ TEA
A41. These are always nosing in the jam. ~ CARS
A42. To draw. ~ HAUL
A43. This is the way the rent looked. ~ TORN
A44. Beastly noises. ~ ROARS
A46. This man gained his fame by degrees. ~ FAHRENHEIT
A48. What millionaires live in. ~ EASE
A49. This furnishes all the information. ~ DATA
A50. These are free for all. ~ SEAS
A51. A high-stepper. ~ SKI
A52. This often leads a merry chase. ~ HARE
A53. This comes from the tall timbers. ~ MAST
A54. Like. ~ AS
A55. This brings out the stars. ~ ENCORE
A57. This is when good fellows get together with a little punch. ~ BOUT
A58. Either. ~ OR
A59. A necktie. ~ NOOSE
A60. Cleo made this years ago. ~ MARC
A61. This helped in the signing of the Boulder Dam Bill. ~ INK
A62. These always run the ranch. ~ WESTERNERS

D1. This is good for the flu. (Abbr.) ~ DR
D2. These have open countenances and will swallow anything. ~ CROCODILES
D3. This is a large bird with its tail gone. ~ TURK
D4. This is an old-fashioned hotel. ~ INN
D5. This is a bone. (But don't try to gamble with it.) ~ OS
D6. Plane surfaces. ~ AREAS
D7. A musical pipe. ~ REED
D8. An affirmative adverb that often makes a conjunction. ~ YES
D9. What some people do with flowers. ~ SAY
D10. Where Herbert Hoover will soon be. ~ IN
D13. What high-fliers become these days. ~ FAMOUS
D14. This is a busy bunch. ~ SWARM
D16. What cigarettes will do for the younger generation. ~ BURN
D17. What Al Jolson's jokes have become. ~ SOBS
D18. These are coaxed along by midnight lunches. ~ NIGHTMARES
D19. To praise. ~ LAUD
D20. This is what the Romans used to put over. ~ TOGO
D22. These buds are just coming out. ~ DEBUTANTES
D23. This is what Cleopatra might have called Antony. ~ TONY
D24. These are always getting tied up. ~ BOWS
D25. This is a good thing to do with a fur coat in warm weather. ~ SHED
D27. This is quite unusual. ~ RARE
D28. You will find these in Hor. No. 20. ~ HOPS
D29. This is quite correct. ~ TRUE
D32. What some people swallow very easily. ~ APPLESAUCE
D34. What an open house does. ~ AIRS
D35. Sometimes this is bad taste. ~ SOUR
D36. A fairy in Persian mythology. ~ PERI
D38. This is one way to reduce. ~ PARE
D39. This is laughable. ~ HAHA
D40. You might get a kick from these. ~ TOES
D41. A place to go for diversion. ~ CASINO
D42. This is opposed to love. ~ HATE
D43. A demonstrative pronoun. ~ THAT
D45. The way the poet made the bucket. ~ OAKEN
D46. The dust that is collected on street cars. ~ FARE
D47. Where two black crows had a falling out. ~ NEST
D49. Ventures. ~ DARES
D52. A pair of lightweights ready for boxing. ~ HOSE
D53. This is rather early for a poet. ~ MORN
D54. A place where they preserved pairs. ~ ARK
D56. This is a milk concern. ~ COW
D57. Where the Scotch used to be lavish. ~ BAR
D58. A good place to keep your shirt. ~ ON
D60. This is some more ego. (Same as Hor. No. 37). ~ ME
D61. Exists. ~ IS


